{"t": 1794114015.441673, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "**Root cause of the red `main` pipeline**\n\nPipeline [#8812](https://gitlab.com/acme/billing-legacy/-/pipelines/8812) (`main`, `a91c2e0`) failed in job `test:contract` (job 77104). The contract test `contract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format` encodes the Finance ERP import requirement (FIN-77): the sequence part of an invoice number must be zero-padded to 6 digits.\n\n```\nassert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\nE  AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\n`billing/invoice.py` was formatting the sequence without padding:\n\n```python\nreturn f\"INV-{year}-{seq}\"\n```\n\n**Fix**\n\nZero-pad the sequence to 6 digits, leaving the `INV-<year>-` prefix unchanged:\n\n```python\n# Finance ERP import (FIN-77): sequence part is zero-padded to 6 digits.\nreturn f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\n`invoice_number(2026, 42)` now returns `INV-2026-000042`. Sequences longer than 6 digits are not truncated (`1234567` stays `1234567`), and the existing prefix/year behaviour is unchanged. I re-ran the contract assertion locally against the patched module and it passes.\n\nSince this MR is the invoice-format change, please rebase it on this fix so the ERP v2 work builds on a green `main`."}, "ok": false}
{"t": 1794114019.5057316, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"project_id": "acme/billing-legacy", "merge_request_iid": "12", "body": "Root cause of the red `main` pipeline: pipeline #8812 (`main`, a91c2e0) failed in job `test:contract` (77104). The contract test `contract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format` encodes the Finance ERP import requirement (FIN-77): the sequence part of an invoice number must be zero-padded to 6 digits.\n\n```\nassert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\nE  AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\n`billing/invoice.py` was formatting the sequence without padding (`f\"INV-{year}-{seq}\"`).\n\nFix applied:\n\n```python\n# Finance ERP import (FIN-77): sequence part is zero-padded to 6 digits.\nreturn f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\n`invoice_number(2026, 42)` now returns `INV-2026-000042`; sequences longer than 6 digits are not truncated, and the prefix/year behaviour is unchanged. The contract assertion passes locally against the patched module.\n\nSince this MR is the invoice-format change, please rebase it on this fix so the ERP v2 work builds on a green `main`."}, "ok": true}
